+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   **Precision Thresholds**: Sphere tracing requires a small convergence threshold $\epsilon$ (e.g., $0.001$) to terminate without infinite loops [S1].
+*   **Lipschitz Guarantee**: The step size $t \leftarrow t + d$ is guaranteed not to penetrate the surface because the SDF satisfies the Lipschitz condition with constant 1 .
+*   **Depth Accuracy**: PDDF sampling accuracy degrades far from the surface, necessitating iterative refinement to converge to the true boundary [S5].
+*   **Visibility Checks**: Directions yielding $\xi(p, v) = 0$ (occluded or invalid) must be filtered to avoid sampling inside geometry or invalid regions [S5].
